Windows Registry Editor Version 5.00

; WorshipPlanner — REMOVE the local-dev Automatic Fullscreen policy keys.
; Right-click -> "Merge" as administrator (or double-click and approve the UAC
; prompt), then FULLY restart Chrome/Edge (use chrome://restart). This deletes both
; the per-user (HKCU) and machine-wide (HKLM) keys for Chrome AND Edge, undoing every
; fullscreen .reg you installed. Use this for the controlled test: with the policy
; gone, confirm the per-display "Go fullscreen" buttons STILL work (they use gesture
; delegation, which should not need the policy) — if they do, the reg file was never
; load-bearing and can be dropped.
;
; A leading "-" on the key path means "delete this key".

[-HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome\AutomaticFullscreenAllowedForUrls]

[-HKEY_LOCAL_MACHINE\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge\AutomaticFullscreenAllowedForUrls]

[-HKEY_CURRENT_USER\SOFTWARE\Policies\Google\Chrome\AutomaticFullscreenAllowedForUrls]

[-HKEY_CURRENT_USER\SOFTWARE\Policies\Microsoft\Edge\AutomaticFullscreenAllowedForUrls]
